##Kevin "KD" Dorsey
You can't fight your way out of stress. 

It doesn't work. 

We all go through really stressful periods in life. It happens. It's actually part of what makes being a human, a human. 

Bad stuff is going to happen. 

What we tend to do when things get hard is WE push harder and harder. 

Do more and more and more.

Without realizing what we were doing/allowing is what has caused the stress in the first place. 

Something has to change. 

But when you are stressed. 

When you are running yourself into the ground....

The ideas of change won't be there for you. In fact the idea of change will sound so hard that you won't even consider it. 

You'll. Just. Do. More. 

Take a breath. 

Take a moment. 

Take a day.

Be open to RECEIVING vs CHASING. See what ideas come to you. See what people pop into your head as a resource. See what happens when you're open to receiving vs just pushing. 

It's unreal what shows up for me when I go into receiving mode. 

Was talking with a good friend of mine, great founder/owner, leader, they are on a trip, but also are going through a tough/rough patch, and this was my exact advise. 

I asked if they were able to unplug at all on this trip and they said no because things were tough. 

I said Pause. Remember you get better BECAUSE you unplug, not because you don't. I alos sounds easier than it is, but sometimes letting go for even a day opens up ideas, space, opportunities you see before. 

Grab a cigar. Grab a coffee. Grab a notebook, and see what shows up. 

I hope he does it, because I know things will show up for him. 

I hope YOU all do it, because I know things will show up for you too. 
